<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Piero Soderini</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1452–<a href="/years/1522">1522</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Piero Soderini was a Florentine statesman elected gonfaloniere of justice for life in 1502, leading the republic restored after the expulsion of the Medici in 1494. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niccolo-machiavelli">Niccolò Machiavelli</a> as his secretary he created a citizen militia. When Spanish troops sacked Prato in 1512 he fled into exile, and the Medici returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/piero-soderini.jpg" alt="Piero Soderini" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ridolfo del Ghirlandaio · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piero_Soderini_(1450-1522),_by_Ridolfo_del_Ghirlandaio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
